.TH ALPHADICT 1 "2026-11-06" "AlphaDict 1.4.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
AlphaDict \- lightweight dictionary for the open .aldict format
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B AlphaDict
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B AlphaDict
is a lightweight dictionary application that reads dictionaries in the open
.B .aldict
format.  It searches the dictionaries installed under
.I /usr/share/alphadict/dicts
and offers lookups from a headword index, a vocabulary book and, under X11,
on-screen word capture.
.PP
The program takes no command line options.  It is configured from its own
settings window; the settings are stored per user and the default
configuration is copied there on first start.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.AlphaDict/configure.xml
Per-user settings, created from
.I /usr/share/alphadict/configure.xml.in
on first start.
.TP
.I ~/.AlphaDict/
Also holds the vocabulary book.
.TP
.I /usr/share/alphadict/dicts/
Every
.I *.aldict
file in this directory is loaded as a dictionary.  A small English-Chinese
sample dictionary is installed here.
.TP
.I /usr/share/alphadict/doc/
Dictionary format documentation.
.TP
.I /usr/share/alphadict/tools/
Python scripts that convert third-party dictionaries (Cedict, StarDict,
dicts.info, IDP) to the AlphaDict XML front-end format.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR AldConvert (1)
.PP
The format of the XML front-end files is described in
.I /usr/share/doc/alphadict/front-end_format.xml
and the dictionary format itself in
.I /usr/share/doc/alphadict/dictionary_inner.pdf
